<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24841" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭŏlē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰόλη.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A daughter of Eurytus</i>, <i>king of
				Œchalia</i>, <i>whom Hercules</i>, <i>after killing Eurytus</i>, <i>married
				to his son Hyllus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 9, 140</span></i>; <i><span class="en">278</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">394</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
			35</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The name of a female slave</i>, <i><span class="en">Prop. 4</span></i>
			(5), 5, 35.</div>
